 "endpoints": {
  "primary": "rare_recall, mean Hungarian-matched recall over the true classes below sqrt(n), paired by data set, on the rare subset",
  "secondary": [
   "ARI",
   "NMI",
   "ACC",
   "many_to_one_ACC",
   "n_clusters",
   "n_balls",
   "n_rare_cores",
   "n_fragment_edges",
   "wall time"
  ],
  "paired_delta": "MG-GBC minus ARP-GB on the same data set, same k, same preprocessing.",
  "agreement": "The two partitions are called identical when their adjusted Rand index is 1 to within 1e-12."
 },
 "preregistered_criteria": {
  "H1_rare_recall": "On the rare subset, the median paired delta rare_recall is greater than 0 and the two-sided exact sign test over the non-tied pairs gives p < 0.05.",
  "H2_noninferiority": "On the rare subset, where the edit can act, the median paired delta ARI is at least -0.05 and no single data set loses more than 0.15 ARI. The same two numbers over the whole cohort are reported beside them; the criterion is stated on the rare subset because the whole-cohort median is dominated by control data sets on which the two partitions are identical by construction.",
  "H3_locality": "On the locality control, where no class is below sqrt(n), the two methods return identical partitions on at least 90% of the data sets. This is the empirical counterpart of the manuscript's locality-of-the-edge-edit proposition (Section 3.4): with no rare core to retain, the edit is empty.",
  "H4_loss_mechanism": "Every rare-subset data set with delta ARI below -0.05 retains at least one rare core, as the locality corollaries of Section 3.4 predict: a loss requires a core admitted inside a dense majority region.",
  "reporting_rule": "All four criteria are reported whether or not they are met. No criterion, no margin, no subset rule and no cohort membership is redefined after the run. The run happens once; the runner refuses to overwrite an existing result file."
 },
 "pre_registration_caveat": "Cohort membership reads no class-rarity quantity. The class count enters only as C >= 2, a task-validity bound: a data set with one class has no partition to recover. The smallest class size is read once, after the cohort is fixed, to place each member in the rare subset or in the locality control; that placement is the manuscript's own rare band and not a configuration choice. Three design decisions were taken before any model was fitted on any candidate data set, and are recorded here. (i) The first version of this screen made the smallest class a membership condition. A walk over ids 1-1560 then filled its primary cohort with twelve data sets from three sources padded by their variant families (leaf, one-hundred-plants-margin/shape/texture, volcanoes-a2..e5), which is a weaker cross-source claim than an unfiltered cohort; membership was therefore made label-free. (ii) The second version took the first 120 admissible data sets in ascending id order. That cohort filled at id 1069 and held 2 rare-subset members out of 120, because an ascending prefix of OpenML is its oldest uploads, dominated by balanced sets, rather than a sample of the repository; membership was therefore made a seeded permutation of the id block. (iii) The third version stopped that permutation at 60 admitted data sets, a cap set by a power calculation on the rare fraction measured in the second walk. The cap was removed before any candidate was scored: with no cap the cohort is the whole admissible population of the block, so its size is a property of the repository rather than a parameter, and the rare subset is whatever the block contains. The realised cohort has 95 members over 10000 draws, 9 in the rare subset and 86 in the locality control, over 95 distinct sources. The floors of 6 rare and 20 control members are capability floors fixed before the draw, not expectations: 6 is the shortest subset on which the two-sided exact sign test behind H1 can reach p < 0.05 at all, its smallest attainable value on six non-tied pairs being 2/2^6 = 0.031, so on a rare subset that short H1 can be met only by an unbroken run of wins and is reported as it comes out. The full screen log, including every drawn id and its skip reason, is written to results/openml_heldout_screen_log.json, and the logs of the first two superseded designs are kept beside it as results/openml_heldout_screen_log_labelfiltered_v0.json and results/openml_heldout_screen_log_ascending_v1.json, so all three cohorts can be reconstructed; the third design was stopped mid-walk when its cap was removed and wrote no log. Restricting the rare subset to the declared domain is a scope statement, not evidence of accuracy outside it: the locality control is what tests the outside."
}